Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: JetBrains Mono Nerd Font (Nerd Fonts 3.5.1) and the iA Writer fonts
Source: https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/download/v3.5.1/JetBrainsMono.zip
 https://github.com/iaolo/iA-Fonts (commits c6588670c71e9ac628acc27b72cde4bf12726b7f and
 b337fe1a4c93026268f70e4b2678371f3e89e2ce)
Comment: The orig tarball holds the Nerd Fonts release zip JetBrainsMono.zip whole and the
 16 iA Writer TTF files by their basenames; packages/fonts/sources.list in the
 @DISTRO_NAME@ repository lists each file's URL and SHA-256.

Files: JetBrainsMono.zip
Copyright: 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors (https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono)
 2016-2026 Ryan L McIntyre and the Nerd Fonts contributors (the patching)
License: OFL-1.1-no-RFN
Comment: JetBrains Mono 2.304 patched by Nerd Fonts 3.5.1 with icon glyphs. The zip's
 OFL.txt, copied below, declares no Reserved Font Name, which is why the Nerd Fonts
 project labels the patched fonts "OFL-1.1-no-RFN" and the family keeps the name
 "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font". The icon glyphs come from the icon sets the zip's README.md
 lists with their own licenses: Codicons and Font Awesome (CC BY 4.0), Devicons,
 Hack's extra glyphs, Font Awesome Extension, Octicons, Seti, Powerline Extra, Powerline
 Symbols and Power Symbols IEC (MIT), MaterialDesign (Apache 2.0), Pomicons (OFL 1.1 with
 RFN), Weather Icons (OFL 1.1) and Font Logos (no license stated). Only the four faces
 JetBrainsMonoNerdFont-{Regular,Bold,Italic,BoldItalic}.ttf are installed.

Files: iAWriterMonoS-*.ttf iAWriterQuattroS-*.ttf iAWriterDuoS-*.ttf iAWriterDuospace-*.ttf
Copyright: 2018 Information Architects Inc. with Reserved Font Name "iA Writer"
 2017 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex" (the IBM Plex typeface the iA Writer
 fonts derive from)
License: OFL-1.1
Comment: The LICENSE.md file next to each family in iaolo/iA-Fonts (identical for the
 four families at the two commits named above) is copied below. The repository's
 README.md adds usage guidelines beyond the license: credit iA Writer when using the
 fonts outside text editors, and do not bundle them with a text editor or make them a
 text editor's default typeface.

Files: debian/*
Copyright: 2026 santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>
